|passage=the '''material''' elements of the universe}}
# Of, relating to, or affecting [[physical]] [[well-being]]; [[corporeal]]; [[bodily]].
#: {{ant|en|spiritual}}
#: {{ux|en|'''material''' needs}}
# {{lb|en|logic}} Of or relating to the [[matter]] of [[reasoning]], as distinguished from the [[form]] of it, especially [[empirical]].
#: {{ux|en|'''material''' cause}}
#: {{ux|en|the '''material''' aspect of being}}
# {{lb|en|especially|law}} Having real [[importance]] or great [[consequence]]s; [[significant]]; [[substantial]].
#: {{ant|en|immaterial}}
#: {{ux|en|found a '''material''' difference between two things}}
#: {{ux|en|You've made several '''material''' contributions to this project.}}
#: {{ux|en|This is the most '''material''' fact in this lawsuit.}}
#* {{RQ:Evelyn Diary|10 March 1685|passage=discourse, which was always '''material''', not trifling}}
#* {{RQ:Locke Human Understanding|2|3|text=I shall, in the account of simple ideas, set down only such as are most '''material''' to our present purpose.}}
# Relating to or concerned with what is purely [[physical]] rather than [[intellectual]] or [[spiritual]], especially excessively so; [[materialistic]].
#: {{ux|en|the '''material''' world}}
#: {{ux|en|interested only in '''material''' progress}}
#: {{ux|en|Don't let '''material''' concerns get in the way of living a happy life.}}
